<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — Morphometric validation: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1413-1589) now reports 14 metrics with references and dispersion statistics: lambda_c = 0.4726 (exact), WT tip Pearson r = 0.9903 (p ~ 1e-5) and Horton-Strahler R_b, generational angle RMSE 2.92 deg, Spry1-/- and bead ratios, hypoplasia ratio 0.3125 (ref 0.4), specimen 12/6 tips, plus six Pass 3 metrics (noise-seeded staircase agreement 0/4, necking index 0.2025, dihedral 90.0 deg (ref 90), Grem1-/- 0.4375 (ref 0.08), Fgf7-/- 1.00 (ref 0.70), Bmp4+/- 1.8125 (ref 1.20)), all bitwise deterministic across two runs. The honesty control is credited for being reported rather than hidden. Deductions: the band-seeded \"4/4 exact mode matches\" metric is circular and the honest control scores 0/4 (-6); angle RMSE is self-referential because half-angles are prescribed from the same table (L856) (-4); the Watanabe & Costantini generation table and the perturbation means (28.5, 5.2, 21.0 tips; 0.88/0.12 fractions) and the Pearson reference 0.9985 are not traceable to a figure or table (-5); three new stromal ratios miss their qualitative references by 2-5x and Spry1-/- overshoots 3.875 vs 2.19 after removing hand-placed buds (-5); the necking index has no reference value; conditions use different RNG streams (SHA-256 of the condition name, L719) so WT vs mutant are not seed-matched (-2); the 90 deg dihedral match is guaranteed by the orientation assumption (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L1438–L1450: Noise-seeded staircase gives [2, 3, 5, 5] vs band map [1, 2, 3, 4]: the Pass 2 4/4 metric was conditioned on its seed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L1438-L1450>",
        "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L719–L719: Per-condition RNG seed = SHA-256 digest of the condition name; WT vs perturbation comparisons are not seed-matched <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L719-L719>",
        "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L856–L859: Prescribed generational half-angles make the angle-RMSE metric self-referential <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L856-L859>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-bmp4-reduced-stromal-inhibition-e12-5-tip-ratio-vs-wt-ectopic-supernumerary-budding>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-e11-0-e13-5-wild-type-ureteric-bud-tip-count-correlation-pearson-r-vs-watanabe-costantini-2004>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-fgf7-stromal-growth-factor-loss-e12-5-tip-ratio-vs-wt>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-gdnf-and-prr-ub-hypoplastic-e12-5-ureteric-tip-reduction-ratio-vs-wt-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-generational-ureteric-bifurcation-angle-rmse-across-e11-5-e13-5-vs-no-sink-ablation-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-grem1-stromal-bmp-de-repression-failure-e12-5-tip-ratio-vs-wt>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-mean-dihedral-rotation-angle-between-successive-splitting-planes-anisotropic-dome-cascade-4-generations>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-ampulla-necking-index-of-the-wt-dichotomous-cap-1-r-cleft-r-lobe>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-noise-seeded-ampulla-tip-splitting-peak-count-agreement-with-the-band-map-1-2-3-4-honesty-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-segmented-e12-5-mouse-metanephros-gfp-ureteric-bud-tip-count-panel-a-wild-type-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-segmented-e12-5-mouse-metanephros-wt-to-mutant-ureteric-tip-multiplicity-ratio-panel-a-vs-panel-b>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-spry1-hyper-branching-exogenous-gdnf-bead-supernumerary-e12-5-tip-count-ratio-vs-wt-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-ureteric-ampulla-tip-splitting-mode-transition-accuracy-across-rho-tip-pi-r-tip-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-wild-type-gdnf-ret-homogeneous-steady-state-signaling-r-2-g-critical-turing-wavelength-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — MorphoEval overall 83.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3 remediated) evaluation of `2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py` (down from 92.1/100 in Pass 2). Both Pass 2 remediation items were closed as honestly labelled reduced models: a 1D Lagrangian moving-boundary necking solver on the ampulla dome with linear short-axis selection and a 90 deg period-2 dihedral cascade (`simulate_moving_boundary_ampulla_necking`, `select_splitting_axis`, `dihedral_rotation_cascade`, Panels H-I, Lean Law 5), and an explicit stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 gain law gamma_eff = gamma (1 + k_F7 FGF7)/(1 + k_B BMP/(1 + k_G GREM1)) with spatial stromal fields that now drive per-tip ampulla radius and splitting multiplicity (`stromal_signaling_gain`, Panel G, Lean Law 4), replacing the Pass 2 prescribed multiplicities and hand-placed side buds. The remediation exposed defects Pass 2 scored over: the band-seeded cap solver seeds the cosine mode it then detects (noise-seeded control 0/4), the hypoplasia set (b = 0.45) has Tr J_0 > 0 and is outside the Turing regime, generational bifurcation half-angles are hard-coded to the reference table (angle RMSE 2.92 deg is self-referential), the Watanabe & Costantini generation table and the perturbation means are not traceable to a figure, the new stromal benchmarks are qualitative encodings the model misses (Grem1-/- 0.44 vs 0.08, Fgf7-/- 1.00 vs 0.70, Bmp4+/- 1.81 vs 1.20) and Spry1-/- overshoots (3.875 vs 2.19). The specimen (SHA-256 locked, 12 WT vs 6 mutant tips) is unchanged; its ground truth is the Pass 1 agent's own count. 5 Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys), 9 self-test suites, 14 bitwise deterministic measurements. Overall 83.8/100 (faithfulness 81.4, reproducibility 89.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py at 028758bc, image/png, 709770 B, 1992×1932 px, artifact_sha256 818d1b74f25bf359339b3bb4f553b254ee38435cc9e836d37f4e53acd0367e10 (sha256 818d1b74f25bf359339b3bb4f553b254ee38435cc9e836d37f4e53acd0367e10), spec_fingerprint f29be7f1600499fda53bd2dbabe454bd253465ad82fc249a5ca7afb434d430b0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: f29be7f1600499fda53bd2dbabe454bd253465ad82fc249a5ca7afb434d430b0; artifact_sha256: 818d1b74f25bf359339b3bb4f553b254ee38435cc9e836d37f4e53acd0367e10; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json=a15b7c6b44319cfd..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg=3264f509ba3a6686..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/paper_citations.bib=698d3f067b082cc3..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/scout_manifest.json=c55304eda64bfba4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-kidney-ureteric-bud-gdnf-ret-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Menshykau & Iber (2013): a Schnakenberg-type GDNF-RET receptor-ligand reaction-diffusion system on the ureteric epithelium has a homogeneous steady state R* = a + b, G* = b/(a + b)^2 and a Turing instability whose fastest mode on the ampulla selects elongation, bifurcation or trifurcation as the tip radius grows | Watanabe & Costantini (2004): time-lapse of cultured E11.5 kidneys shows predominantly dichotomous (with some trichotomous) ampulla splitting and generation-dependent tip counts and branch angles | Basson et al. (2005): Spry1-/- kidneys hyper-branch with supernumerary buds; exogenous GDNF beads induce ectopic budding | Michos et al. (2004), Qiao et al. (1999), Miyazaki et al. (2000): Grem1-/- fails ureteric outgrowth, Fgf7-/- reduces ureteric growth and nephron number, Bmp4+/- shows ectopic budding (qualitative) | Menshykau et al. (2012), Metzger et al. (2008): branch-mode selection depends on the local geometry of the growing tip; successive lung bifurcation planes rotate ~90 deg (orthogonal bifurcation); reconstructed_in_script: Steady state, dispersion relation, lambda_c and (a, b) phase space; 1D Neumann ampulla-cap IMEX solver with band-seeded and noise-seeded initial conditions; 1D Lagrangian moving-boundary necking of the dome; linear two-lobe axis selection on an anisotropic dome and a dihedral cascade; 2D self-avoiding ureteric tree coupled to GDNF sink, BMP, Gremlin1 and FGF7 Gaussian fields with per-tip stromal gain feeding R_tip -> rho_tip -> splitting multiplicity; 7 genetic/bead conditions plus no-sink, equal-diffusion and stromal-ablation controls; GFP specimen segmentation and tip counting; transfer_boundary: The 3D phase-field/ALE item is closed only as a 1D moving boundary on the dome plus a linear axis-selection argument; no surface tension, curvature, re-meshing or E13.5-E16.5 calyx stage; the 90 deg dihedral follows from an explicit daughter-orientation assumption (daughter_long_axis_parallel=True), not from the dynamics | Stromal constants k_B = 3.0, k_G = 4.0, k_F7 = 0.8, BMP baseline 0.5 and the Gaussian field amplitudes/widths are model-scale calibrations, not measured rate constants; BMP4 and BMP7 share a single field; ligand fields are quasi-static per generation | The band-seeded mode staircase [1, 2, 3, 4] is conditioned on its own cosine initial condition; the noise-seeded honesty control gives [2, 3, 5, 5]; does_not_claim: Quantitative reproduction of Grem1-/-, Fgf7-/- or Bmp4+/- tip counts (the reference ratios 0.08/0.70/1.20 are qualitative encodings); 3D ampulla shape; derivation of bifurcation angles from the PDE (half-angles are prescribed per generation); a kidney-specific dihedral distribution; verification offline of the 5 new DOIs." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py:1204 and datasets JSON genetic_and_bead_perturbation_benchmarks — the hypoplasia set (a = 0.10, b = 0.45) has Tr J_0 > 0 and is outside the Turing regime yet still drives the Gdnf+/- tree; choose a hypoplasia parameterisation inside the Turing band (e.g. reduce gamma or b to a value with Tr J_0 < 0, det J_0 > 0) and re-source it.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py:1575-1585 — verify the Song et al. (2013) PLoS ONE attribution of the Wikimedia specimen and replace the agent-counted 12/6 ground truth with a published count or state that the reference is an annotator count.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py:272-310 — remove or repair `compute_turing_phase_space` (sigma_proxy multiplies a term by 0.0 at L299 and the function is never called).",
        "remediation needed: 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py:367-383 and 1614-1617 — the band-seeded cap solver seeds the cosine mode of the band-predicted m and Suite 4 / measurement 2 then \"detect\" it (noise-seeded control gives [2, 3, 5, 5], 0/4). Re-derive the band map from the fastest Neumann mode on the dome (or a 2D/3D cap) so the two-lobe mode is the selected mode, and make the self-test assert the noise-seeded result.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py:544-585 — the 90 deg dihedral follows from `daughter_long_axis_parallel = True`; make the daughter dome orientation an output of the moving-boundary solver (orientation of the necked lobes) and vendor a kidney dihedral distribution (Short et al. 2014) rather than the lung 90 deg reference.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py:719 and 726-728 — seed-match WT and perturbation trees (shared RNG stream) and expose/sweep `gain_wt_ref`, `g_ref`, `size_jitter_sd`, `R_TIP_WT_DEFAULT`, `TIP_RADIUS_SIGNAL_EXPONENT` or document their derivation.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py:774-789 and 1478-1501 — the stromal benchmarks are qualitative encodings (Grem1-/- 0.08, Fgf7-/- 0.70, Bmp4+/- 1.20) that the model misses by 2-5x (0.4375 / 1.00 / 1.8125); separate BMP7 from BMP4, add ligand turnover ODEs instead of quasi-static Gaussians, and replace the encoded ratios with digitised counts from Michos 2004 / Qiao 1999 / Miyazaki 2000 or mark the metrics unscored.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py:856-862 — generational bifurcation half-angles 51/42.5/41-1.4g deg are hard-coded to the Watanabe & Costantini table, so measurement 4 (angle RMSE 2.92 deg) and Panel F are self-referential. Derive the daughter directions from the cap peak positions or the local GDNF gradient.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json:175-307 — the Watanabe & Costantini generation table, the perturbation means (28.5, 5.2, 21.0 tips; 0.88/0.12 fractions) and the Pearson reference 0.9985 cite no figure/table; pin each value to a figure/table/page or mark them as agent-constructed and drop them from scored metrics.",
        "remediation needed: morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_054_kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret.lean:122-126 — extend `tip_splitting_peaks` to the m = 4 polydomain band so Law 3 covers the full Python band map." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.38e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The parameter space is substantially richer: rho_tip sweeps across four regimes with two seeding modes (`evaluate_tip_splitting_regimes`, L445-472), 7 genetic/bead conditions (WT, Gdnf+/-, Spry1-/-, GDNF bead, Grem1-/-, Fgf7-/-, Bmp4+/-) plus no-sink, equal-diffusion and stromal-ablation controls (`evaluate_all_conditions_and_generations`, L945-1057), a daughter-dome aspect-ratio sweep for axis selection (Panel I, L1349-1362) and a dihedral ablation (L1023), and the CLI exposes `--a-ret --b-gdnf --gamma --d-ratio --generations --seed --k-bmp --k-grem --k-fgf7 --no-stroma` (L1676-1685), all wired through `render_outputs(stromal_overrides=...)` into every tree call and the GIF (L1687-1702). Deductions: the generational bifurcation half-angles are hard-coded (L856) so the branch-angle axis of the morphospace is not parameter-controlled (-5); `gain_wt_ref`, `g_ref = 0.60`, `size_jitter_sd = 0.08` (L726-728), `R_TIP_WT_DEFAULT` and `TIP_RADIUS_SIGNAL_EXPONENT` (L102-103) and the `r_tip *= 0.92` cascade decay (L577) are fixed calibrations not exposed or swept (-4); the Bmp4+/- `bmp_scale = 0.75` is an assumption (-2); no sweep shows the staircase flipping under `--k-*` (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L726–L728: gain_wt_ref, g_ref, size_jitter_sd fixed model-scale calibrations placed to hit rho_WT ~ 2 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L726-L728>",
        "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L856–L862: base_half_deg hard-codes 51/42.5/41-1.4g half-angles; no-sink ablation only scales by 0.62 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L856-L862>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`self_test()` (L1596-1668) runs 9 suites in ~1.5 s: SHA-256 integrity, Lean Laws 1-2 identities, equal-diffusion ablation, IMEX modes, tree perturbation ordering (hypo < WT < bead < Spry1), specimen 12 vs 6, stromal law and ordering (Suite 7), necking/dihedral/axis selection/rho_flip (Suite 8) and two-run bitwise determinism of all 14 metrics (Suite 9); per-condition seeding is a SHA-256 digest of the condition name (L719), replacing Pass 2's process-salted `hash()`; the default render takes 1.74 s and regenerates the PNG and 6-frame GIF; `requirements.lock.txt` pins the venv (Python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0). Deductions: the comparison PNG is gitignored (`*.png`) so the committed artifact is the GIF only (-3); Suite 4 still asserts the band-seeded staircase rather than the noise-seeded result, so the self-test encodes the circular check (-3); no byte-level SHA of the rendered PNG/GIF is asserted (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L1614–L1617: Suite 4 asserts the band-seeded staircase [1, 2, 3, 4], not the noise-seeded honesty control <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L1614-L1617>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-repro-package-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — Source and data traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/` vendors the SHA-256-locked specimen and reference JSON (verified at runtime, `verify_dataset_integrity`, L123-156), the JSON gained `stromal_feedback_module_pass3` (L308-355) and `reduced_3d_geometry_pass3` (L356-375) with per-benchmark `obs_note`s stating that the stromal ratios are qualitative encodings and `doi_verified_offline: false` flags, `paper_citations.bib` grew from 6 to 11 entries (Menshykau 2012, Michos 2004, Qiao 1999, Miyazaki 2000, Metzger 2008, Short 2014; L56-121), and the README documents the Pass 3 additions (L25-33). Deductions: the five new DOIs could not be verified offline (-3); the Watanabe & Costantini generation table (JSON L175-260) and the perturbation benchmark means (L261-307) were created in Pass 1/2 and cite no figure/table/page (-5); the specimen's Song et al. (2013) attribution is plausible (PRR UB knockout file title) but unverified (-2); the stromal reference ratios 0.08/0.70/1.20 are the agents' encodings of qualitative phenotypes, not published means (-3); the 90 deg dihedral reference is lung literature applied to kidney without a vendored kidney distribution (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json L175–L307: Watanabe & Costantini generation table and perturbation benchmark means with no figure/table pinpoints <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json#L175-L307>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-locked E12.5 metanephros GFP specimen is segmented as before (`segment_specimen_ureteric_bud`, L1063-1160): green-channel threshold, morphological cleanup, EDT caliber and radial-weighted local maxima recover 12 WT tips in Panel A and 6 mutant tips in Panel B (ratio 2.00), overlaid in the comparison figure, and the nine-panel figure now shows the stromal perturbation bars (G), the necked dome outlines (H) and the axis-selection sweep (I) beside the specimen. Deductions: the \"published\" counts 12 and 6 are the Pass 1 agent's own counts of the image, not numbers from Song et al. (2013), and that attribution (L1575, L1585) is unverified offline (-6); the two new morphologies (necking index 0.20, 90 deg dihedral) have no kidney specimen or vendored distribution to compare against; the 90 deg reference is lung/qualitative (-5); the 2D tree remains a schematic with no shape metric (caliber, ampulla width, inter-tip spacing) compared with the specimen beyond the tip count (-4); the specimen comparison itself is unchanged from Pass 2 so no credit is added for the new geometry (0)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L1575–L1585: Specimen measurement sources attribute the Wikimedia image to Song et al. (2013) PLoS ONE 8(5):e63835 Fig. 2A-C; unverified offline and the 12/6 ground truth is an agent count <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L1575-L1585>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

